{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reserveCapacity"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"minimumCapacity","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"minimumCapacity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The requested number of elements to store.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are adding a known number of elements to an array, use this method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to avoid multiple reallocations. This method ensures that the array has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"unique, mutable, contiguous storage, with space allocated for at least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the requested number of elements.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Calling the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method on an array with bridged storage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triggers a copy to contiguous storage even if the existing storage"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"has room to store ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimumCapacity"},{"type":"text","text":" elements."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For performance reasons, the size of the newly allocated storage might be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"greater than the requested capacity. Use the array’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to determine the size of the new storage.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Preserving-an-Arrays-Geometric-Growth-Strategy","type":"heading","text":"Preserving an Array’s Geometric Growth Strategy","level":1},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you implement a custom data structure backed by an array that grows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dynamically, naively calling the ","type":"text"},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method can lead","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to worse than expected performance. Arrays need to follow a geometric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation pattern for appending elements to achieve amortized","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"constant-time performance. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"text":" type’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"append(_:)"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"append(contentsOf:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods take care of this detail for you, but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" allocates only as much space as you tell it to"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(padded to a round value), and no more. This avoids over-allocation, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can result in insertion not having amortized constant-time performance.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following code declares ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"text":", an array of integers, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"text":" function, which adds ten more values to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array on each call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["  var values: [Int] = [0, 1, 2, 3]","","  \/\/ Don't use 'reserveCapacity(_:)' like this","  func addTenQuadratic() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      values.reserveCapacity(newCount)","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" increases the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values"},{"type":"text","text":" array’s capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by exactly 10 elements on each pass through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addTenQuadratic()"},{"type":"text","text":", which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is linear growth. Instead of having constant time when averaged over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many calls, the function may decay to performance that is linear in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"values.count"},{"text":". This is almost certainly not what you want.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In cases like this, the simplest fix is often to simply remove the call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reserveCapacity(_:)"},{"text":", and let the ","type":"text"},{"code":"append(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" method grow the array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for you."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["  func addTen() {","      let newCount = values.count + 10","      for n in values.count..<newCount {","          values.append(n)","      }","  }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need more control over the capacity of your array, implement your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own geometric growth strategy, passing the size you compute to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"reserveCapacity(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Complexity","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"text":" is the number of elements in the array.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/reserveCapacity(_:)"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reserves enough space to store the specified number of elements."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/array\/reservecapacity(_:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Adding Elements","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/insert(_:at:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/insert(contentsOf:at:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/replaceSubrange(_:with:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Array\/replaceSubrange(_:with:)-7293p"],"anchor":"Adding-Elements"}],"metadata":{"platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","introdu